WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:14.390 align:start position:0%
 
good afternoon  i want to thank the president of the  european commission ursula van der leyen  for her visit to madrid to exchange  views  with the spanish government on the  invasion of ukraine  and its impact on the european economy  her effort is an evidence of the  leadership that the european commission  and its president are showing  at this critical time for europe  and it is precisely in these situations  like the in situations like this when  the leadership of men  and women at the head of institutions  are is valued  today it is more necessary than ever to  exercise our political responsibilities  with the vision of the path to take  with empathy for those who suffer  and with the capacity to work together  all these qualities  are possessed by the president of the  european commission  and i want to reiterate this  a female president  because a few days before the  celebration of march 8  it is pertinent to claim the  contribution of women to politics  and i if i have one thing clear  it is that it is a success and a pride  to have a woman at the head of europe  like ursula van der leyen thank you  president  we have a clear diagnosis of what what  happened  the putin regime  sees the consolidations of the political  project like the european union as a  threat  putin tries to weaken  our european area of prosperity based on  democracy freedom and social justice  and that is why he attacked us  the political project like the european  union as a threat  putin tries to weaken our european area  of prosperity based on democracy freedom  and social justice  and that is why he attacked us  but but but i think he's wrong in my  opinion putin has made two strategic  mistakes  the first  believing that ukraine was going to  simply surrender to the invasion  on the contrary ukrainians are showing  determination in defending their freedom  once again we declare our admiration and  solidarity with the ukrainian people  putin's second mistake  has been to believe  that europe was going to divide  no  europe today is more united and more  determined than ever  in the actions against putin  in solidarity with ukraine  and in the response that europe will  give  to the economic impact that putin's war  has cost  we have discussed all these with the  president of the commission a meeting in  which i have been accompanied by vice  president calvinian vice president  rivera  the government of spain has  conveyed to the commission its  resounding commitment to european unity  the implementation of economic sanctions  also in our offer to continue  transferring humanitarian aid to ukraine  as we are already doing  and finally in our absolute availability  to host refugees as spain has always  done when there has been a humanitarian  crisis president you can count on us  finally  we have addressed the impact that  putin's invasion will have on inflation  the price of energy and raw materials  the president knows that high energy  prices are undermining family economies  impacting smes and industrial companies  and generating inflationary effects  as you know the european commission is  finalizing the second second  communication on energy spain has been  calling for  immediate and forceful measures to  question the impact of gas prices on the  wholesale electricity market  and in this sense president borderline  and i agree on the urgency of taking  measures in the energy field  we have received  a review  some proposals that spain has been  defending to stop this period of energy  prices in the same way we have also  need to advance  more strongly in the field of  interconnections  another point in which there is a  considerable alignment is the need to  strengthen the european union's common  security and defense policy  uh because a strong european defense  will be the perfect complement to an  increasingly relevant nato  and i think that the madrid summit next  june will be an excellent opportunity to  underline the complementary between the  defense policies of both organizations  lastly we have exchanged  opinions on aspects related to the  union's strategic autonomy we share  the need to strengthen our industry and  drive technological development in key  sectors  the urgency to diversify our import and  export market through a renewed trade  policy and to speed up the green and  digital transitions  all of them are major strategic  challenges that we  will have to face in the coming months  and years  but i have no doubt that the european  union once again  will emerge stronger from them so thank  you very much ursula thank you very much  president as you will know  um you can count on spain thank you so  much prime minister dear pedro  i'm very glad to be here in madrid spain  indeed is a key partner for me and i'm  here to prepare with you the informal  summit that we're going to have  next week  and indeed first of all we discussed  today the extremely difficult situation  created by putin's war  the number of refugees already exceeds  1.2 million people  and the number is likely to increase  multiple times in the days and weeks to  come  these are innocent women men and  children who are fleeing putin's  ruthless and brutal war  and they need our immediate assistance  all member states are showing a big  heart and helping as much as they can  and many things pedro for the  offer that you  did in our discussions but also here we  know very well that we can count on you  there is a long tradition and many  thanks for that  i also want to commend the front line  countries like poland romania slovakia  and hungary but also moldova for their  outstanding solidarity  they deserve our solidarity and support  as do all european countries that  welcome refugees  the european union is providing 500  million euros in a first tranche to help  ukrainians  and we made sure this week that  ukrainian refugees  of this terrible war get residency  rights in the european union immediately  for at least a year  so this includes not only the access to  the labor market but for example also  access  to  schools access to medical care many  things that are now desperately needed  and let me say how proud i am of the  european union today  our unity our determination and the  solidarity that is really europe at its  best  we have imposed three packages of  hard-hitting sanctions on the russian  leadership  many thanks pedro here too for the very  close cooperation  by this we are drastically limiting  putin's ability to finance this  atrocious war  but putin's war as you said and its  consequences will also impact our  citizens and our economies here in the  european union  and we have also discussed that today  a one of the critical most critical  topics is indeed energy one thing is  very clear  the european union must get rid of the  dependency of russian oil gas and coal  and for that  we have to diversify the supply  we have to get better at energy  efficiency and we have to massively  invest in renewables  because this is a strategic investment  in our security of supply  but also in the health of our planet  and i'm glad to say that spain is a real  front runner  with your impressive share of renewables  and in the national energy mix the  renewable energies plays the major role  with the large lng capacities  but also with the impressive know-how  and the industrial players in the field  of renewables  so spain can and will play an important  role in supplying europe and for that  we must work indeed on the  interconnections between the iberian  peninsula and the rest of the european  union and we've discussed that we will  work hard on that this is one of the  major priorities a second priority right  now is of course  that we need to help the consumers the  households and the businesses that have  indeed problems with the high energy  bills we discussed that intensively and  it will certainly be a topic on the  informal summit in  versailles  diaper this war  unleashed by putin is not only atrocious  it's also a fight  of our democracies against  autocracy  it is a defining moment in our history  and spain knows very well that democracy  is priceless and that we have to stand  up for it  i'm very much looking forward seeing you  at the summit and many thanks for  hosting me this afternoon thank you so  much  you

